{%- comment -%}
  TALLOW ADVERTORIAL · B24 destination page, rev 2026-07-07 (reverted same day)
  Founder call: the ad headlines themselves already carry the reveal/
  outcome tease (B24's quote-card banners), so the landing page's job is
  to build toward that reveal, not restate it instantly. Reverted to the
  original scene-setting confessional opening. Mid-article CTAs (early,
  post-mechanism-reveal, post-review) are inline blue text links woven
  into the paragraph flow (Javvy/listicle style), not standalone buttons,
  per founder feedback that buttons read "too forward." The closing CTA
  (end of Final Thoughts) and the optional sale/update-box CTA remain
  full buttons, that's the one deliberate hard-sell moment on the page.
  Incoming query string (ad UTMs) is passed through to every CTA link so
  attribution survives ad -> advertorial -> PDP; each CTA also fires a
  labeled custom event (fbq/gtag) for per-position click tracking.

  Assign via page template page.advertorial.json. One destination for all
  B24 creatives (distinct UTMs on the ad side). CTA -> PDP.

  Compliance posture: first-person story is the same narrative persona used
  across the ad account. NO fabricated view counts, NO fake doctor quotes,
  NO invented testimonials: the review slot must only ever hold real
  customer reviews. Disclosure footer included and must stay.
{%- endcomment -%}

